<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds reverse to end weak after U.S. data.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds reverse to end weak after U.S. data.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> July 1998 6.25 pct   103.19/27 (-0.03)   bid yield 3.57 (+0.03)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		114.09/19 (-0.19)		 4.90 (+0.05)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct   99.18/26  (-0.29)		 5.86 (+0.05)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		111.25/45 (-0.52)		 6.58 (+0.05)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June)	 99.88  (-0.23)</p>
<p>TREASURIES (June)  106.56 (-0.78 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1241 (PREV 1.1246)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 -0.01	-0.01	  10-2 yr  229     (230)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.09	-0.11	  10-5 yr   96	(96)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.16	-0.17</p>
<p>-------------------------(April 11)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds reverse to end weak after U.S. March inflation and sales data spooks bond markets with spectre of fresh rate U.S. rate rise in May. Cash flows still absent, dealers say, with yields needing to rise further to tempt back investors.</p>
